[12.342055, "i", "claude --verbose --output-format stream-json -p 'Your task is to create a file /app/src/program.cbl in which there will be a new COBOL program in fixed format, \nwhich will be run from the /app/src directory and should be compiled and executed using GnuCOBOL 3.  \nDo not include \">>SOURCE FORMAT IS FIXED\". Keep each line ≤ 80 characters. The compiler will use fixed format by default.\nThe program will run from /app/src directory and must compile with GnuCOBOL 3. File /app/src/INPUT.DAT already exist.\n  Processes mortgage applications. Checks terms and generates a payment schedule. The program reads the existing file at /app/src/INPUT.DAT.\n  ID - X(10) NAME - X(30) LOAN-AMOUNT - 9(10) PROPERTY-VALUE - 9(10) DOWN-PAYMENT - 9(10) TERM - 9(2) RATE - 9(3)V9(2) separated by the symbol '\"'\"';'\"'\"'.\n  Calculates the minimum down payment (15% of the property value). If the client'\"'\"'s down payment is less, the application is rejected.\n  For approved applications, the monthly payment is calculated using the annuity nom"]
[12.342275, "i", "inal formula and a full payment schedule is generated.\n  The results are written to the file at /app/data/OUTPUT.DAT: ID - X(10) STATUS - X(5) (REASON - X(50) in case of refusal)\n    For rejected applications: ID and reason for rejection.\n    For approved applications: ID and  «APPRO\\n» and detailed payment schedule:\n    MON-NUMBER - 9(3) PAYMENT-AMOUNT, INTEREST-PART, PRINCIPAL-PART - 9(8).99 REMAINING-BALANCE - 9(10).99.(without header).\n    - CALCULATIONS: \n        MIN_DOWN = PROP_VALUE * 0.15\n        MONTHLY_RATE = INTEREST_RATE / 1200\n        MONTHLY_PAYMENT = LOAN_AMOUNT * monthly_rate / (1 - (1 + monthly_rate)**(-term_months))\n        Use ROUNDED for all financial computations.\n  Success Criteria:\n    A correctly constructed payment schedule in the file output. Example output file:\n     «TEST000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\n      TEST000002APPRO\n      001 00000400.00 00000022.92 00000377.08 0000004622.92 etc.»' --allowedTools Bash Edit Write Read Glob Grep LS WebFetch NotebookEdit Not"]
[12.342359, "i", "ebookRead TodoRead TodoWrite Agent; tmux wait -S done\r"]
[12.342494, "o", "claude --verbose --output-format stream-json -p 'Your task is to create a file /app/src/program.cbl in which there will be a new COBOL program in fixed format, \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.342555, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.342808, "o", "which will be run from the /app/src directory and should be compiled and executed using GnuCOBOL 3.  \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.342891, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.343152, "o", "Do not include \">>SOURCE FORMAT IS FIXED\". Keep each line ≤ 80 characters. The compiler will use fixed format by default.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.343278, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.34343, "o", "The program will run from /app/src directory and must compile with GnuCOBOL 3. File /app/src/INPUT.DAT already exist.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.343736, "o", "  Processes mortgage applications. Checks terms and generates a payment schedule. The program reads the existing file at /app/src/INPUT.DAT.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.344021, "o", "  ID - X(10) NAME - X(30) LOAN-AMOUNT - 9(10) PROPERTY-VALUE - 9(10) DOWN-PAYMENT - 9(10) TERM - 9(2) RATE - 9(3)V9(2) separated by the symbol '\"'\"';'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.344311, "o", "  Calculates the minimum down payment (15% of the property value). If the client'\"'\"'s down payment is less, the application is rejected.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.344582, "o", "  For approved applications, the monthly payment is calculated using the annuity nominal formula and a full payment schedule is generated.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.345475, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.345715, "o", "  The results are written to the file at /app/data/OUTPUT.DAT: ID - X(10) STATUS - X(5) (REASON - X(50) in case of refusal)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.34585, "o", "    For rejected applications: ID and reason for rejection.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.345999, "o", "    For approved applications: ID and  «APPRO\\n» and detailed payment schedule:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.346021, "o", "> "]
[12.346273, "o", "    MON-NUMBER - 9(3) PAYMENT-AMOUNT, INTEREST-PART, PRINCIPAL-PART - 9(8).99 REMAINING-BALANCE - 9(10).99.(without header).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.346359, "o", "    - CALCULATIONS: \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.346433, "o", "        MIN_DOWN = PROP_VALUE * 0.15\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.34653, "o", "        MONTHLY_RATE = INTEREST_RATE / 1200\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.346732, "o", "        MONTHLY_PAYMENT = LOAN_AMOUNT * monthly_rate / (1 - (1 + monthly_rate)**(-term_months))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.346755, "o", "> "]
[12.346894, "o", "        Use ROUNDED for all financial computations.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.347002, "o", "  Success Criteria:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.34715, "o", "    A correctly constructed payment schedule in the file output. Example output file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.347375, "o", "     «TEST000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>       TEST000002APPRO\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[12.347758, "o", "      001 00000400.00 00000022.92 00000377.08 0000004622.92 etc.»' --allowedTools Bash Edit Write Read Glob Grep LS WebFetch NotebookEdit NotebookRead TodoRead TodoWrite Agent; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
