[137.654288, "o", "\"stdout\":\"APP0000001DENY  INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nAPP0000002APPRO\\n001 00002316.70 00002291.66 00000025.03 0000004974.96\\n002 00002316.70 00002280.19 00000036.51 0000004938.44\\n003 00002316.70 00002263.45 00000053.24 0000004885.20\\n004 00002316.70 00002239.05 00000077.65 0000004807.54\\n005 00002316.70 00002203.46 00000113.24 0000004694.30\\n006 00002316.70 00002151.55 00000165.14 0000004529.15\\n007 00002316.70 00002075.86 00000240.84 0000004288.31\\n008 00002316.70 00001965.47 00000351.22 0000003937.09\\n009 00002316.70 00001804.50 00000512.20 0000003424.88\\n010 00002316.70 00001569.74 00000746.96 0000002677.92\\n011 00002316.70 00001227.38 00001089.32 0000001588.60\\n012 00002316.71 00000728.11 00001588.60 0000000000.00\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[159.394864, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01Wg9kQrdQE84ifuGh7jAsLh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The program is working. However, looking at the expected output format more carefully, the STATUS field is \\\"DENY \\\" (5 chars with space) but based on the example it should be \\\"DENY \\\" with the reason following after just a space. Let me look at the expected output format again:\\n\\nLooking at the example:\\n```\\nTEST000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nTEST000002APPRO\\n001 00000400.00 00000022.92 00000377.08 0000004622.92\\n```\\n\\nThe format shows:\\n- ID (10 chars) + STATUS (5 chars: \\\"DENY \\\" or \\\"APPRO\\\") + space + REASON for rejections\\n\\nBut I'm outputting an extra space. Let me verify the format more closely and check if there's also an issue with the second record - I see the numbers look different. Let me recalculate:\\n\\nFor the second record:\\n- LOAN_AMOUNT = 5000\\n- TERM = 1 year = 12 months  \\n- RATE = 5.50%\\n- MONTHLY_R"]
[159.395086, "o", "ATE = 5.50 / 1200 = 0.004583...\\n- Expected payment ≈ 428.04 per month\\n\\nBut I'm getting 2316.70. Let me check the parsing - the issue is with how numbers are being parsed. The input shows:\\n```\\nAPP0000002;John Smith Clark              ;0000005000;0000004000;0000003500;01;00550\\n```\\n\\nSo LOAN = 5000, PROPERTY = 4000, DOWN = 3500, TERM = 1 year, RATE = 5.50 (but my PIC is 9(3)V9(2) so 00550 = 005.50).\\n\\nWait, that's wrong - 00550 with PIC 9(3)V9(2) would give 055.00. Let me reconsider the rate format. Looking at the numbers:\\n- First record: 00550 - this is 5.50% interest rate\\n- Second record: 00550 - same\\n\\nSo the input format for rate seems to be 9(3)9(2) where we need to divide by 100 to get the actual percentage. Or maybe it's stored as 9(5) where the last 2 digits are decimal.\\n\\nLet me trace through more carefully. If rate is 00550 and that represents 5.50%, then in my code RATE is 9(3)V9(2) = 055.00, and then I divide by 1200, which gives 0.045833... That's way too high.\\n\\nThe issue is the RATE"]
[159.395158, "o", " format. If 00550 means 5.50%, then it's actually stored as the rate * 100. So I should interpret it as 9(5) and divide by 120000 instead, or fix the parsing.\\n\\nLooking at it again: 00550 likely means rate = 5.50. With PIC 9(3)V9(2), when I read \\\"00550\\\", it would interpret as 005.50, not 055.00. Let me verify this is correct.\\n\\nActually with PIC 9(3)V9(2), the value 00550 would be interpreted as 005.50 (i.e., 5.50%). Then dividing by 1200 gives monthly rate of 0.00458333... That seems correct.\\n\\nLet me recalculate for the second record:\\n- Loan = 5000\\n- Monthly rate = 5.50 / 1200 = 0.00458333\\n- Term months = 12\\n- Payment = 5000 * 0.00458333 / (1 - (1.00458333)^(-12))\\n- = 22.9167 / (1 - 0.9466)\\n- = 22.9167 / 0.0534\\n- = 429.15 approximately\\n\\nBut I'm getting 2316.70. Something is very wrong. Let me debug:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":542,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":28247,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":542,\"ephemeral_1"]
